{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788297741229,"sessionID":"ses_fa1260da9ffea7gMsosoWnpMXr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-afa6e6b0f8d35899","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view 158"},"output":"title:\tDesign and build a streaming pipe-to-subprocess primitive for shell-out calls\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t158\n--\nRuling from the call-syntax-and-outside-world grill round (shell-out-design board row): the maintainer picked **full streaming pipe-to-subprocess** over blocking-capture-only, a bash-style capture literal, or deferring entirely.\n\nMaintainer's note on the pick: \"the bash style capture literal for this full pipe to subprocess flow looks interesting too; but that would probably need to be a template string and if we do build template string then we may as well build universal template strings\" -- flagged as a related idea, tracked separately (see template-strings-design).\n\nShape ratified (from the round's preview, PROPOSED/unverified):\n\n```toylang\nlines | pipe_through(\"grep\", [\"foo\"]) | collect\n```\n\nThis explicitly inherits the open Q35 dependency (plans/questions.md#q35 -- what stdout/stderr are, whether a program writes or returns) since streaming a subprocess's output progressively requires that effect model to exist first. Q35 should land, or at least have a concrete enough shape, before this is implementable.\n\nWritten by the drive-loop coordinator session.\n","metadata":{"output":"title:\tDesign and build a streaming pipe-to-subprocess primitive for shell-out calls\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t158\n--\nRuling from the call-syntax-and-outside-world grill round (shell-out-design board row): the maintainer picked **full streaming pipe-to-subprocess** over blocking-capture-only, a bash-style capture literal, or deferring entirely.\n\nMaintainer's note on the pick: \"the bash style capture literal for this full pipe to subprocess flow looks interesting too; but that would probably need to be a template string and if we do build template string then we may as well build universal template strings\" -- flagged as a related idea, tracked separately (see template-strings-design).\n\nShape ratified (from the round's preview, PROPOSED/unverified):\n\n```toylang\nlines | pipe_through(\"grep\", [\"foo\"]) | collect\n```\n\nThis explicitly inherits the open Q35 dependency (plans/questions.md#q35 -- what stdout/stderr are, whether a program writes or returns) since streaming a subprocess's output progressively requires that effect model to exist first. Q35 should land, or at least have a concrete enough shape, before this is implementable.\n\nWritten by the drive-loop coordinator session.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view 158","time":{"start":1788297741221,"end":1788297741227}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me start by reading the AGENTS.md file and the issue. Let me also check the current state.\n\nLet me start by fetching the issue and reading key files.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ed9ff30001P4hUZNnJnBQt66","sessionID":"ses_fa1260da9ffea7gMsosoWnpMXr","messageID":"msg_05ed9f34c0016uLR45pKYos2AS"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788297741248,"sessionID":"ses_fa1260da9ffea7gMsosoWnpMXr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-976095deaa538893","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git log --oneline -10 && git status"},"output":"7c4cc86 Accept snapshots after merging issue-140\n08b0e56 Integrate issue-140: sum and max builtins over Vec<Int>/Vec<Int64> (gh:140 ruling)\n3b8c0d7 Add sum and max as builtin reductions\n920bd33 Integrate issue-135 and issue-141: the slow-fragment tier, js/py tail calls\nef15c7f Lower self-tail-calls to loops on js and py\nd6a91e5 Grow the docs harness a slow-fragment tier\nb8ad5b6 Integrate issue-133: restore the Euler 8/11/13/18 docs pages\nba9dff7 Restore the Euler 8/11/13/18 docs pages\nd9443ff Migrate draft.md's intro sections to a docs overview page\n411e55f Migrate draft.md's intro sections to an overview page\nOn branch issue-158\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\n","metadata":{"output":"7c4cc86 Accept snapshots after merging issue-140\n08b0e56 Integrate issue-140: sum and max builtins over Vec<Int>/Vec<Int64> (gh:140 ruling)\n3b8c0d7 Add sum and max as builtin reductions\n920bd33 Integrate issue-135 and issue-141: the slow-fragment tier, js/py tail calls\nef15c7f Lower self-tail-calls to loops on js and py\nd6a91e5 Grow the docs harness a slow-fragment tier\nb8ad5b6 Integrate issue-133: restore the Euler 8/11/13/18 docs pages\nba9dff7 Restore the Euler 8/11/13/18 docs pages\nd9443ff Migrate draft.md's intro sections to a docs overview page\n411e55f Migrate draft.md's intro sections to an overview page\nOn branch issue-158\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git log --oneline -10 && git status","time":{"start":1788297741245,"end":1788297741247}},"id":"prt_05eda0074001iK90ItPmw7Y6eU","sessionID":"ses_fa1260da9ffea7gMsosoWnpMXr","messageID":"msg_05ed9f34c0016uLR45pKYos2AS"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788297742831,"sessionID":"ses_fa1260da9ffea7gMsosoWnpMXr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-82504264473daf4b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"just --list"},"output":"Available recipes:\n    check          # The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\n    checks         # The repo's mechanical checks, the same surface the Stop hook runs.\n    clippy         # Run clippy with the repo's lint set, the same surface the Stop hook checks.\n    default        # List available recipes.\n    drive          # The autonomous drive loop: a tick every 600s, live colorized output, Ctrl-C to stop. Run ONE.\n    euler-data DIR # `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\n    fmt            # Formatter check over every .toy file from the repo root down (exit 1 on drift).\n    fmt-write      # Rewrite drifted files in place (same exit code as the check).\n    peek           # Watch the current coordinator tick live (detaches with Ctrl-C, tick untouched).\n    slow-test      # this is where the deferred execution claim is re-verified.\n    test           # The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\n    tick           # Fire one coordinator tick right now (zero tokens if there is nothing to do).\n","metadata":{"output":"Available recipes:\n    check          # The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\n    checks         # The repo's mechanical checks, the same surface the Stop hook runs.\n    clippy         # Run clippy with the repo's lint set, the same surface the Stop hook checks.\n    default        # List available recipes.\n    drive          # The autonomous drive loop: a tick every 600s, live colorized output, Ctrl-C to stop. Run ONE.\n    euler-data DIR # `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\n    fmt            # Formatter check over every .toy file from the repo root down (exit 1 on drift).\n    fmt-write      # Rewrite drifted files in place (same exit code as the check).\n    peek           # Watch the current coordinator tick live (detaches with Ctrl-C, tick untouched).\n    slow-test      # this is where the deferred execution claim is re-verified.\n    test           # The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\n    tick           # Fire one coordinator tick right now (zero tokens if there is nothing to do).\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"just --list","time":{"start":1788297742828,"end":1788297742830}},"id":"prt_05eda039f001znUXuTuDe1EFX7","sessionID":"ses_fa1260da9ffea7gMsosoWnpMXr","messageID":"msg_05ed9f34c0016uLR45pKYos2AS"}}
