{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788297767483,"sessionID":"ses_fa1260da9ffea7gMsosoWnpMXr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-ba2575c93e83c63f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat Cargo.toml"},"output":"[package]\nname = \"toylang\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\n\n[dependencies]\nanyhow = \"1.0.104\"\ninkwell = { version = \"0.10.0\", features = [\"llvm22-1\"] }\nmlua = { version = \"0.12.0\", features = [\"lua54\", \"vendored\", \"anyhow\"] }\nserde_json = \"1.0.151\"\ntempfile = \"3.27.0\"\nwinnow = \"1.0.4\"\n\n[dev-dependencies]\ninsta = \"1.48.0\"\nserde = { version = \"1.0.229\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_norway = \"0.9.42\"\n\n# build.rs reuses the parser (winnow) to check prelude.toy at build time; see build.rs itself.\n[build-dependencies]\nwinnow = \"1.0.4\"\n\n# The three lints the quality hooks forward; thresholds live in clippy.toml.\n# On in the manifest so plain `cargo clippy` sees them: the Stop hook adds\n# nothing of its own. See plans/quality-practices.md.\n[lints.clippy]\ncognitive_complexity = \"warn\"\ntoo_many_lines = \"warn\"\nfn_params_excessive_bools = \"warn\"\n","metadata":{"output":"[package]\nname = \"toylang\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\n\n[dependencies]\nanyhow = \"1.0.104\"\ninkwell = { version = \"0.10.0\", features = [\"llvm22-1\"] }\nmlua = { version = \"0.12.0\", features = [\"lua54\", \"vendored\", \"anyhow\"] }\nserde_json = \"1.0.151\"\ntempfile = \"3.27.0\"\nwinnow = \"1.0.4\"\n\n[dev-dependencies]\ninsta = \"1.48.0\"\nserde = { version = \"1.0.229\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_norway = \"0.9.42\"\n\n# build.rs reuses the parser (winnow) to check prelude.toy at build time; see build.rs itself.\n[build-dependencies]\nwinnow = \"1.0.4\"\n\n# The three lints the quality hooks forward; thresholds live in clippy.toml.\n# On in the manifest so plain `cargo clippy` sees them: the Stop hook adds\n# nothing of its own. See plans/quality-practices.md.\n[lints.clippy]\ncognitive_complexity = \"warn\"\ntoo_many_lines = \"warn\"\nfn_params_excessive_bools = \"warn\"\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cat Cargo.toml","time":{"start":1788297767478,"end":1788297767482}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"This is a large task. I need to understand the architecture: how `lines`, `collect`, streams work across 6 backends (go, jq, js, llvm, lua, py, rs? let me check). Actually there are emit_go, emit_jq, emit_js, emit_llvm, emit_lua, emit_py, emit_rs, emit_toylang.\n\nLet me understand the architecture. This is a big task - implementing a new primitive `pipe_through` across all backends. Let me look at the structure of the codebase first.\n\nLet me look at how `lines` and `collect` are implemented. Let me search for `lines` and `collect` in src.\n\nGiven the complexity, let me use the explore agent to map out the architecture thoroughly.\n\nActually, let me first understand the key files. Let me look at src/lib.rs, ast.rs, tir.rs, and how lines/collect are handled.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05eda663c001fo6v6kPRyUGVcJ","sessionID":"ses_fa1260da9ffea7gMsosoWnpMXr","messageID":"msg_05eda4d1d001QucfbMXJwrf5VF"}}
