{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788297872642,"sessionID":"ses_fa1260da9ffea7gMsosoWnpMXr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_77f65dfb49c14e8b980b8ab2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rln \"pipe_through\\|shell-out\\|shell_out\\|subprocess\" plans docs draft.md research-log 2>/dev/null | head -30"},"output":"plans/benchmark-tooling-spike.md\nplans/board.yaml\nplans/crate-simplification.md\nplans/prototype_1_5.md\nplans/prototype_1_5_step_4.md\ndocs/adr/0004-backends-emit-source-run-by-real-toolchains.md\ndraft.md\nresearch-log/streaming-input-is-pull-verified-against-jq-itself.md\n","metadata":{"output":"plans/benchmark-tooling-spike.md\nplans/board.yaml\nplans/crate-simplification.md\nplans/prototype_1_5.md\nplans/prototype_1_5_step_4.md\ndocs/adr/0004-backends-emit-source-run-by-real-toolchains.md\ndraft.md\nresearch-log/streaming-input-is-pull-verified-against-jq-itself.md\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -rln \"pipe_through\\|shell-out\\|shell_out\\|subprocess\" plans docs draft.md research-log 2>/dev/null | head -30","time":{"start":1788297872636,"end":1788297872640}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So `refuses: true` is for cases where the program legitimately fails at runtime (division by zero, unwrap of none, invalid input). These are refusals, not \"unsupported backend features\".\n\nFor `pipe_through`, the point is that it works on the backends that can do subprocesses. jq literally cannot. Hmm.\n\n\n\nWait, let me look at this from a different angle. Maybe the design intent is that pipe_through for jq is implemented by... hmm. Let me search the plans for \"shell-out\" and \"pipe_through\" to find design docs about how the subprocess is implemented per backend.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05edc04df0015L8MyhkJ9KzCzt","sessionID":"ses_fa1260da9ffea7gMsosoWnpMXr","messageID":"msg_05edbf873001JzbYhGY6meSunf"}}
