 Hmm. But wait, the ratified shape is literally `pipe_through(\"grep\", [\"foo\"])`. How does this language spell multi-arg calls? Let me check if there are multi-arg functions... `join(\", \")`? From draft: \"join(\", \")\" — hmm, that might be `join(\", \")` with one arg (a string with a comma? no...). Let me check the prelude and how join_lines is spelled. Actually the corpus case uses `join_lines collect lines` - `join_lines` with one arg. Let me look at the prelude.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ede4cd0001MDKInGaYQO4GcE","sessionID":"ses_fa1260da9ffea7gMsosoWnpMXr","messageID":"msg_05ede3f65001Y6e2npsRvabLkq"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788298022112,"sessionID":"ses_fa1260da9ffea7gMsosoWnpMXr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_7d594fd2887c41f3a4723dac","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"join\" src/check/mod.rs | head; echo \"=====\"; grep -rn \"join\" tests/corpus/*.yaml | head -10"},"output":"349:/// -- under eager lowering the emitted expression genuinely is the joined string every backend\n580:                named.join(\" and \"),\n581:                qualified.join(\" or \")\n1041:            missing.join(\" and \")\n1137:                                missing.join(\" and \")\n=====\ntests/corpus/char_range_and_complement.yaml:2:# (kantord/toylang#96): `and` joins the two bounds and `not` is the complement. Both used to be\ntests/corpus/enum_recursive_extracted.yaml:5:# has to survive that: Lua decided from it whether to emit its join helper at all, and emitted a\ntests/corpus/fizzbuzz_arms.yaml:6:  join_lines(\ntests/corpus/fizzbuzz.yaml:3:  join_lines(\ntests/corpus/join_basic.yaml:1:# join is join_lines' sibling with no separator, both prelude.toy source rather than per-backend\ntests/corpus/join_basic.yaml:5:  join([\"ada\", \"bo\"])\ntests/corpus/join_lines_one.yaml:1:# join_lines is prelude.toy source now, not a per-backend builtin -- pinned on two backends of\ntests/corpus/join_lines_one.yaml:5:  join_lines([\"only\"])\ntests/corpus/jsonlines_scalars.yaml:1:# The minimal form: no record spreading, no nesting, just per-element JSON encoding joined by\ntests/corpus/lines_cat.yaml:3:# stream becomes an ordinary Vec; `join_lines` and printing are unchanged from every other program.\n","metadata":{"output":"349:/// -- under eager lowering the emitted expression genuinely is the joined string every backend\n580:                named.join(\" and \"),\n581:                qualified.join(\" or \")\n1041:            missing.join(\" and \")\n1137:                                missing.join(\" and \")\n=====\ntests/corpus/char_range_and_complement.yaml:2:# (kantord/toylang#96): `and` joins the two bounds and `not` is the complement. Both used to be\ntests/corpus/enum_recursive_extracted.yaml:5:# has to survive that: Lua decided from it whether to emit its join helper at all, and emitted a\ntests/corpus/fizzbuzz_arms.yaml:6:  join_lines(\ntests/corpus/fizzbuzz.yaml:3:  join_lines(\ntests/corpus/join_basic.yaml:1:# join is join_lines' sibling with no separator, both prelude.toy source rather than per-backend\ntests/corpus/join_basic.yaml:5:  join([\"ada\", \"bo\"])\ntests/corpus/join_lines_one.yaml:1:# join_lines is prelude.toy source now, not a per-backend builtin -- pinned on two backends of\ntests/corpus/join_lines_one.yaml:5:  join_lines([\"only\"])\ntests/corpus/jsonlines_scalars.yaml:1:# The minimal form: no record spreading, no nesting, just per-element JSON encoding joined by\ntests/corpus/lines_cat.yaml:3:# stream becomes an ordinary Vec; `join_lines` and printing are unchanged from every other program.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -rn \"join\" src/check/mod.rs | head; echo \"=====\"; grep -rn \"join\" tests/corpus/*.yaml | head -10","time":{"start":1788298022110,"end":1788298022111}},"id":"prt_05ede4cd3001faE6kITrhXVLuU","sessionID":"ses_fa1260da9ffea7gMsosoWnpMXr","messageID":"msg_05ede3f65001Y6e2npsRvabLkq"}}
